  "query_preview": "/MONDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 141 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nThe stalled upper low will sink towards Iowa on Tuesday and its dry \nslot will rode the midlevel clouds and allow for some of the stratus \nto mix out. The cold front will exit the area in the early morning \nand add to the mixing potential with CAA. Post-frontal storms will \nbe possible as low-level lapse rates steepen and will contribute to \nthe gusty winds that afternoon. Storms could trend stronger if the \ndry slot comes more north into the state, allowing for lapse rates \nin the midlevels to steepen out once more. Wednesday and \nThursday have trended colder. This is because the upper low will\npark right over Iowa Wednesday and all but guarantee stratus \nand rain until the TROWAL departs late Thursday. Highs may very \nwell trend down and into the 40s. Highs will recover back into \nthe 50s and 60s once the flow resumes a southerly component.",
